{"id":"CVE-2001-0572","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2001-07-27T04:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-08T04:21:38.923Z","description":"The SSH protocols 1 and 2 (aka SSH-2) as implemented in OpenSSH and other packages have various weaknesses which can allow a remote attacker to obtain the following information via sniffing: (1) password lengths or ranges of lengths, which simplifies brute force password guessing, (2) whether RSA or DSA authentication is being used, (3) the number of authorized_keys in RSA authentication, or (4) the lengths of shell commands.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.linux-mandrake.com/en/security/2001/MDKSA-2001-033.php3","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_MANDRAKE"],"name":"MDKSA-2001:033"},{"url":"http://www.redhat.com/support/errata/RHSA-2001-033.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2001:033"},{"url":"http://archives.neohapsis.com/archives/bugtraq/2001-03/0225.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20010318 Passive Analysis of SSH (Secure Shell) Traffic"},{"url":"http://distro.conectiva.com.br/atualizacoes/?id=a&anuncio=000391","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_CONECTIVA"],"name":"CLA-2001:391"},{"url":"http://www.kb.cert.org/vuls/id/596827","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_CERT-VN"],"name":"VU#596827"}],"vendors":["openssh"]}
